`verilator_config
// lint_waivers.vlt -- one line per waiver: the rule, where it applies, and above it, the reason.
// From the guide, section 7.
// SPEC.md, Memory map: index = (addr >> 2) mod WORDS. The other address bits are unused by design.
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL -file "*rv32i_imem.sv" -match "*'addr'*"
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL -file "*rv32i_dmem.sv" -match "*'addr'*"
// TODO: two warnings remain (funct7 bits, mem_read in rv32i_core.sv).
//       Find out what each signal was meant to do before you waive it.
//       One of them bears on the security question (guide section 8).
